  "verdict": "At the tuned physical target the light doublet has no tree-level coupling to any heavy mode, so lambda_eff equals the direct H quartic, 1 for the certified couplings; one-loop running then gives m_h ~ 173 GeV, which excludes this coupling point. Because bounded-below along the pure-H ray needs lambda_direct >= 0, every coupling point of this family without portal feedback has m_h >= 133.6 GeV at one loop; the sufficient BFB floor 2 beta^2 costs only another ~1.2 GeV. Reaching 125 GeV needs a negative GUT-scale matching contribution of about -0.03 (one loop), from heavy exchange through portals that vanish in the benchmark or from loop thresholds. G3 stays open; the model is not excluded."
